WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.900
Every time you work on a local app,

00:01.980 --> 00:06.900
are you still remembering numbers like…
127.0.0.1… port 3000?

00:07.300 --> 00:10.200
Why make local development
harder than it needs to be?

00:10.500 --> 00:12.900
With Locly, it starts with just one line.

00:13.500 --> 00:16.300
Install it with a single command…
and you're ready.

00:16.760 --> 00:19.900
Then open the user interface,
add your local services,

00:20.000 --> 00:22.600
and give each one a name
you can actually remember.

00:22.940 --> 00:27.550
Instead of 127.0.0.1…
you get app.local.

00:27.580 --> 00:31.300
No domain registration.
No complicated DNS setup.

00:31.840 --> 00:33.900
And when you want more control as a developer,

00:34.100 --> 00:36.500
Locly also gives you a terminal interface.

00:37.450 --> 00:41.200
Add, edit, enable, or remove services
with simple commands…

00:41.400 --> 00:44.300
and even use JSON
for automation and AI tools.

00:44.600 --> 00:47.700
Everything stays local, simple, and organized.

00:48.000 --> 00:52.900
Locly.
Remember names, not numbers.
